#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#	Content Blocks - t3sbootstrap's processed values inside frontend.html
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#	EXT:content_blocks renders every element through a FLUIDTEMPLATE inheriting
#	from lib.contentBlock. t3sbootstrap's fields - padding, margin, "extra class",
#	background - are attached to tt_content via addToAllTCAtypes, so they already
#	show up in a content block's form. They were just never evaluated: that is the
#	BootstrapProcessor's job, and it only ran under lib.contentElement.
#
#	This set adds it to lib.contentBlock as well, so frontend.html gets the same
#	variables as t3sbootstrap's own templates:
#
#	  {classAttr}    ready-made class="..." from padding, margin and "extra class"
#	  {styleAttr}    ready-made style="..." from background color and "extra style"
#	  {styleInline}  the same style as a rule for a <style> block
#	  {class}        the classes only, with a leading space
#	  {trimClass}    the same classes without the leading space
#	  {header}       classes and alignment of the heading
#	  {parentCType}  CType of the container, if the element sits in one
#
#	Example in frontend.html:
#	  <div id="c{data.uid}"{classAttr -> f:format.raw()}{styleAttr -> f:format.raw()}>
#
#	Copied, not rebuilt: the processor's settings live once under lib.contentElement
#	and stay in sync automatically.
#
#	Order matters. EXT:content_blocks registers its own processor at 10 and replaces
#	data with a ContentBlockData object there. FlexFormProcessor and BootstrapProcessor
#	access data like an array, so they have to run BEFORE 10, while data is still the
#	raw tt_content row.
#
lib.contentBlock {
	dataProcessing {
		# t3sbootstrap's FlexForm - the processor reads its configuration from it.
		5 < lib.contentElement.dataProcessing.5
		6 < lib.contentElement.dataProcessing.224
	}
}
